  "id": "Compound::DB00396 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Progesterone is linked to Abcb1 through a series of molecular interactions involving steroid hormones and their binding to transporters. The evidence suggests that Progesterone, through its role in causing conditions like Pelvic Venous Thrombosis, Endometrial Hyperplasia, and Dermatitis Hemorrhagic, indirectly influences Abcb1 via steroid hormones. Estriol, Toremifene, and Estrone, all steroid hormones, bind to Abcb1, indicating a potential mechanism by which these hormones modulate Abcb1 activity. The lowest common ancestors of these pathways—Steroid and Oxo Steroid—highlight the involvement of steroid hormones in the overall process. While the exact mechanism linking Progesterone to Abcb1 remains indirect, the shared pathway through steroid hormones suggests a broader regulatory role of these compounds in cellular transport. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Progesterone may influence Abcb1 through its effects on steroid hormone levels, which in turn modulate Abcb1 function.",
